                            CONTRIBUTING
Changes require an RFC (request for comments) before a PR. Post your proposal to
the engineering team at contact@podomy.com.

This includes new subsystems, protocol changes, and architectural
decisions. PRs opened without a prior group discussion will be redirected there
before code review.

Use GitHub Issues for bugs and actionable tasks. Tag issues with
good-first-issue if they are suitable for newcomers.

                         Review Expectations

Small PR (bugfix)       3 business days
Normal PR               7 days
RFC                     7 days

If maintainers cannot meet the window, they will say so. Silence is
not a no.

                          Getting Started
Prerequisites  Go 1.12.x, dep, autoconf, cmake, and a C++ toolchain.
               Toolchain check: ./build/go-version-check.sh go

The supported build excludes proprietary code. The CCL-licensed
enterprise tree (pkg/ccl and friends) has been removed from this fork;
the full `cockroach` binary target does not exist here. Build the OSS
binary instead:

1. Build        make buildoss   # full build needs C++ deps; see build/README
2. Test         make test       # or go test on the package you touched
3. Pick an issue or go over the code

4. Send an RFC to contact@podomy.com if the change is not small
5. Submit a PR
